#. Tag: title
#: introduction.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "សេចក្តី​ណែនាំ"

#. Tag: title
#: introduction.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is &krita;?"
msgstr "តើ​ &krita; ជា​អ្វី​?"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:7
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "&krita;, part of &koffice;, can do everything you want with images "
#| "&mdash; or it will be able to one day. Everything from photo retouching, "
#| "image editing, and last but not least creating original art on your "
#| "computer as if you were working with real paint and brushes, pencils, pen "
#| "and ink. Every day &krita; becomes a little better, a little more useful. "
#| "We are working on it, anyway. We, that is, Adrian, Bart, Boudewijn, "
#| "Casper, Cyrille, Michael and Sven. It could be you, too &mdash; whether "
#| "you would like to help with some artwork for the user interface, cool "
#| "ideas for the todo, helpful bug reports, usability reviews or even actual "
#| "code, you will not be snubbed by us."
msgid ""
"&krita;, part of &koffice;, can do everything you want with images &mdash; "
"or it will be able to one day. Everything from photo retouching, image "
"editing, and last but not least creating original art on your computer as if "
"you were working with real paint and brushes, pencils, pen and ink. Every "
"day &krita; becomes a little better, a little more useful. We are working on "
"it, anyway. We, that is, \\Bart, Boudewijn, Casper, Cyrille, Lukas, Sven and "
"others. It could be you, too &mdash; whether you would like to help with "
"some artwork for the user interface, cool ideas for the todo, helpful bug "
"reports, usability reviews or even actual code, you will not be snubbed by "
"us. Join us on our mailing list (kimageshop-devel@kde.org) or on irc &mdash; "
"#koffice@freenode.net."
msgstr ""
"&krita; ជា​ផ្នែក​មួយ​នៃ​កម្មវិធី &koffice; វា​អាច​ឲ្យ​អ្នក​ធ្វើការ​ជាច្រើន​លើ​រូបភាព &mdash; ។ អ្វីៗ​"
"ដែល​បាន ​មក​ពីការ​កែកុន​រូបថត ការកែសម្រួល​រូបភាព ប៉ុន្តែ​មិន​បង្កើត​សិល្បៈ​ដើម​នៅ​លើ​កុំព្យូទ័រ​រ​បស់​អ្នក​​ បើ​អ្នក​"
"កំពុង​ធ្វើ​ការ​ជា​មួយ គូរ ច្រាស ខ្មៅ​ដៃ ប៉ិច​ និង​​ទឹកខ្មៅ ។  &krita; កាន់​តែ​មាន​លក្ខណៈ​ប្រសើរ​ឡើង មាន​"
"អត្តប្រយោជន៍​ច្រើន​ឡើងៗ​ជា​រៀង​រាល់​ថ្ងៃ ។ ឥឡូវ​យើង​កំពុង​ធ្វើ​ការ​ជាមួយយ​វា ។យើង​ទាំងអស់​រួម​មាន , "
"Adria, Bar, Boudewij, Caspe, Cyrill, Michaelនិងd Sve ។.ពេល​ខ្លះ​វា​ក៏​អាច​ជា​អ្នក​ដែរ នៅ​"
"ពេល​ដែល​អ្នកត្រូវ​ការ​ជំនួយ​ដែល​ត្រូវ​ការ ការងារ​សិល្បៈ​ធ្វើ​ជា​ចំណុច​ប្រទាក់ វា​ពិត​ជា​គំនិត​ដ៏​វិសេស​មួយ​សម្រាប់​ធ្វើ​ "
"របាយការណ៍​កំហុស,ចំពោះ​ការ​ពិនិត្យ​ឡើង​វិញ​ដែល​ពោរពេញ​ទៅ​ដោយ​អត្ថប្រយោជន៍នោះ ឬកូដរបស់​​អ្នកនឹង​មិន​ត្រូវ​បាន​"
"បង្រួម​ឲ្យ​ខ្លី​ដោយ​ពួក​យើង​ឡើយ ។."

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&krita; is as much yours as it is ours. It should be fun, innovative, and "
"experimental &mdash; first and foremost a pleasure to use and to hack on."
msgstr ""
"&krita; ភាគ​ច្រើន​ជា​របស់​អ្នក ក៏​ដូច​ជា​របស់​យើង​ដែរ ។ វា​គួរ​តែ​ល្អ ការកែប្រែ និង​ការពិសោធន៍​ជាលើក​"
"ដំបូងហើយ​វា​ក៏​សំខាន់​សម្រាប់​ប្រើ​ដើម្បីជួសជុល​កម្មវិធី​កុំព្យូទ័រ ។"

#. Tag: title
#: introduction.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "Key features"
msgstr "លក្ខណៈ​ពិសេស​"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "The most important features &krita; currently has to offer, are:"
msgstr "លក្ខណៈ​ពិសេស​សំខាន់​បំផុតរបស់ &krita; បច្ចុប្បន្ន​ផ្តល់​ជូន​ដូច​ខាង​ក្រោម​នេះ ៖"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:32
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Plugins: Krita is extensible through plugins. There are tools, "
#| "colorspaces, paint operations, filters and kpart-based user interface "
#| "plugins."
msgid ""
"Plugins: &krita; is extensible through plugins. There are tools, brush "
"engines colorspaces, paint operations, filters, pixel generators and generic "
"user interface plugins."
msgstr ""
"កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ ៖ Krita ដែល​ពង្រីក​តាម​កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ ។ មាន​ឧបករណ៍​ជាច្រើន​ដូចជា  គំរូ​ពណ៌ប្រតិបត្តិការ​គូរ និង​"
"កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ​ចំណុច​ប្រទាក់​អ្នក​ប្រើ​មាន​មូលដ្ឋាន​លើ​ kpart ។"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Scriptable: &krita; is scriptable in Python and Ruby using Kross, the cross "
"language scripting engine that originated in Kexi. The scripting is "
"compatible with PyQt/KDE and Korundum for adding GUI items, such as dialog "
"boxes."
msgstr ""
"Scriptable ៖ &krita; ជាស្គ្រីប​ដែល​អាច​ប្រើ​ក្នុង​ Python និង Ruby ប្រើ Kross កាត​តាម​ម៉ាស៊ីន​"
"ស្ទ្រីប​ភាសា ដែល​ត្រូវធ្វើ​ឲ្យ​ក្លាយ​ជា​ភាសា​ដើម​នៅ​ក្នុង Kexi ។ ការស្គ្រីប​​ដែល​ឆប​គ្នាជាមួយ PyQt/KDE "
"និង Korundum សម្រាប់​បន្ថែម​ធាតុ​ GUI ជា​ច្រើន​ដូច​ជា ប្រអប់ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:41
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Color models: &krita; uses lcms for a dependable color workflow using icc "
#| "profiles for importing, exporting, selecting paint colors, printing, "
#| "cutting and pasting. 8, 16, and 32 bit colorspaces are available (RGB, "
#| "CMYK, L*a*b*, ...) and colors can be selected from a color wheel, rgb or "
#| "grayscale sliders or with a palette."
msgid ""
"Color models: &krita; uses lcms for a dependable color workflow using icc "
"profiles for importing, exporting, selecting paint colors, printing, cutting "
"and pasting. 8, 16, and 32 bit colorspaces are available (RGB, CMYK, "
"L*a*b*, ...) and colors can be selected from a color wheel, rgb or grayscale "
"sliders or with a palette. Krita also supports OpenCTL based colorspace "
"plugins and custom colorspace plugins, for instance the painterly "
"colorspaces that support mixing colors in a realistic way."
msgstr ""
"ម៉ូដែល​ពណ៌ ៖ &krita; ប្រើ​ lcms សម្រាប់​លំហូរ​ការងារ​ពណ៌​ដែល​អាច​ទុក​ចិត្ត​បាន​ប្រើទម្រង់​ icc នាំចូល​ "
"នាំចេញ ការជ្រើស​ពណ៌ ការ​បោះពុម្ព ការ​កាត និង​ការ​បិទ​ភ្ជាប់ ។ គំរូ​ពណ៌ដែល​អាច​រក​បាន​ ៨ ១៦ និង​ ៣២ ប៊ីត​ "
"(RGB, CMYK, L*a*b*, ...) និង​ពណ៌​ជាច្រើន​ដែល​អាច​ជ្រើស​ពីពណ៌ rgb ឬ​គ្រាប់​រំកិលមាត្រដ្ឋាន​ប្រផេះ ឬ ​"
"លំនាំ​ពណ៌​ស ។"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:50
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Editing and viewing: Unlimited undo and redo are available. You can cut, "
#| "copy and paste between lagers and images, with conversion through icc "
#| "profiles if this is necessary. OpenGL is supported for display. The view "
#| "can be made fullscreen and can be split. Rulers are available, the image "
#| "can be zoomed, and for maximizing the workspace all palette windows can "
#| "be hidden in one go. Also a histogram palette is available."
msgid ""
"Editing and viewing: Unlimited undo and redo are available. You can cut, "
"copy and paste between layers and images, with conversion through icc "
"profiles if this is necessary. OpenGL is supported for display. The view can "
"be made fullscreen and can be split. Rulers are available, the image can be "
"zoomed, and for maximizing the workspace all palette windows can be hidden "
"in one go. Also a histogram palette is available."
msgstr ""
"ការ​កែសម្រួល និង​ការ​មើល ៖ អាច​ប្រើបាន​ មិន​ធ្វើ​វិញ និង​ធ្វើ​វិញ​គ្មាន​ព្រំដែល​ ។ អ្នកអាច​កាត់ ចម្លង​ និង​បិទ​"
"ភ្ជាប់​រវាង​រូបភាពធំៗ ជា​មួយ​ការ​បម្លែង​តាម​ទម្រង់ icc បើ​វា​ចាំបាច់ ។ OpenGL ត្រូវ​បាន​គាំទ្រ​សម្រាប់​"
"បង្ហាញ ។ អាច​មើល​ពេញ​អេក្រង់ ហើយ​អាច​បំបែក​បាន ។iបន្ទាត់​អាច​ប្រើ​បាន រូបភាព​ក៏​អាច​ពង្រីក និងកា​រពង្រីក​"
"អប្បរមា​តំបន់ការងារ​ បង្អួច​លំនាំដើម​ទាំងអស់​អាច​លាក់ ។gលំនាំអ៊ីស្ត្រូក្រាម​ក៏​អាច​ប្រើ​បាន ។le."

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Images and layers: Layers and entire images can be mirrored, sheared, "
"rotated and scaled, converted between colorspaces, and layers in different "
"colorspaces can be merged. An image can be separated into colorspace "
"channels."
msgstr ""
"រូបភាព​ និង​ស្រទាប់ ៖ ស្រទាប់​ និងរូបភាព​ទាំងមូលចអាច​បញ្ចាំង កាត់ បង្វិលនិង​ធ្វើ​មាត្រដ្ឋាន បម្លែង​រវាង​គំរូ​"
"ពណ៌ និង​ស្រទាប់​តាម​គំរូ​ពណ៌​ដែល​ខុស​គ្នា​អាច​ដាក់​បញ្ចូល​គ្នាបាន ។រូបភាព​អាច​បំបែក​ជា​ឆានែល​គំរូ​ពណ៌ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:62
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Layers: Layers can be added, removed, grouped, locked, made (in)visible, "
#| "and re-ordered. Adjustment layers (layers which perform a filter "
#| "function) can be added as well. A layer can be saved as a separate image "
#| "and its colorspace can be changed."
msgid ""
"Layers: Layers can be added, removed, grouped, locked, made (in)visible, and "
"re-ordered. Filter layers (layers which perform a filter function) can be "
"added as well. A layer can be saved as a separate image and its colorspace "
"can be changed. There are clone layers that copy all or part of a layer to "
"another place in the layer stack. There are vector layers that allow you to "
"combine your raster images with rich text, vector graphics and even, though "
"KOffice's plugin system, musical notation or charts."
msgstr ""
"ស្រទាប់ ៖ ស្រទាប់​ជាច្រើន​អាច​បន្ថែម​ យក​ចេញ ដាក់ជាក្រុម ចាក់សោ ​មើល​ឃើញ មើល​មិន​ឃើញ និងតម្រៀប​តាម​"
"លំដាប់ ។ លៃតម្រូវ​ស្រទាប់ (ស្រទាប់​ដែល​បង្ហាញ​មុខងារ​តម្រង) ក៏​អាច​បន្ថែម​បាន​ដែរ ។ ស្រទាប់​មួយ​អាច​"
"រក្សាទុក​ជា​បំណែក​រូបភាព​ ហើយ​គំរូពណ៌​របស់​វា​ក៏​អាច​ផ្លាស់ប្តូរ​ផង​ដែរ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Masks: masks can be applied to a layer. There are transparency masks, for "
"masking out a part of a layer, filter masks that apply a filter to part of a "
"layer, and local selection masks that constrain editing on a layer to a "
"selection without actually hiding anything."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Brush engines: &krita; comes with a collection of brush engine plugins, some "
"mimic classical paint tools such as are familiar to anyone who has used an "
"electronic paint application, others are programmable, and others again try "
"to mimic traditional media."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tools: there are tools to make it easy to paint lines, ellipses and other "
"shapes, as well as a full complement of selection tools. Painting tools can "
"be constrained by guides that make it easy to paint shapes in a natural-"
"looking way, without being overly neat."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:88
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Filters: &krita; can multithread the operation of some filters. Filters "
#| "can be previewed in the filter gallery. Available filters include color "
#| "adjustment, sharpen or blur, emboss, raindrops, and more."
msgid ""
"Filters: &krita; can multithread the operation of some filters. Filters are "
"previewed on the image canvas itself instead of in a small preview window. "
"Available filters include color adjustment, sharpen or blur, emboss, "
"raindrops, and more. There is also a category of plugins called \"generators"
"\", which can programmatically fill an area or a layer with pixels."
msgstr ""
"តម្រង ៖ &krita; អាចជា​ប្រតិបត្តិការ​នៃ​តម្រង​មួយ​ចំនួន ។ តម្រង​អាច​មើ​ល​ជា​មុន​នៅ​ក្នុងវិចិត្រសាលតម្រង ។ "
"តម្រង​អាច​រក​បាន​រួមមាន​ការ​លៃតម្រូវ​ពណ៌ ច្បាស់ ឬ​ព្រិល ក្រឡោត ដំណក់ទឹក​ភ្លៀង ។"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:95
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Brushes: The GIMP brush shapes can be used, both colored and grayscale "
#| "brushes and pipe brushes. Custom brushes can be created, even from entire "
#| "layers or images. Colored brushes can also be used as masks."
msgid ""
"Brushes: Gimp brush shapes can be used, both colored and grayscale brushes "
"and pipe brushes. Custom brushes can be created, even from entire layers or "
"images. Colored brushes can also be used as grayscale brushes."
msgstr ""
"ច្រាស ៖  រាង​ច្រាស​របស់ GIMP អាច​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើទាំងច្រាស​ពណ៌ និង​ច្រាស​មាត្រដ្ឋាន និង​បំពង់​ច្រាស ។ច្រាស​"
"ផ្ទាល់​ខ្លួន​អាច​ត្រូវ​បាន​បង្កើត ពី​ស្រទាប់​ ឬ​រូបភាព​ទាំងមូល ។ ដ្រាស​ដាក់ពណ៌អាច​ប្រើ​ជារបាំង ។"

#. Tag: title
#: introduction.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color management"
msgstr "ការ​គ្រប់គ្រង​ពណ៌"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One of the most distinguishing features in &krita; is its color management. "
"If you put two screens side to side, you will notice that there is often a "
"lot of difference in the way they display colors. Even white, especially "
"white, is often not the same thing at all. On one screen it can be a dirty "
"yellow, on another screen a sickly bluish. Very seldom is it a creamy milk-"
"white. The same holds, unfortunately, for scanners, printers and digital "
"cameras. So, if you want to see the right colors on screen and on paper, "
"being the colors that you saw when taking your snapshot, you will have to "
"compensate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&krita; can do this for you: in &krita;, a color is (almost) never just a "
"set of numbers, one for each color channel; it is a set of numbers with "
"information attached. And that extra information is contained in a profile: "
"your image has a profile, your scanner has a profile, your camera should "
"have a profile and your screen has a profile. When passing information from "
"your image to your screen, the profiles are checked and the correct color is "
"computed. This may cause a little slowness, now and then, but the result is "
"that you can work with colors, instead of almost meaningless RGB triplets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Available colorspaces are: 8 bit/channel RGB, CMYK, grayscale, 16 bit/"
"channel RGB, CMYK, grayscale and L*a*b*, <quote>half</quote> RGB, and 32 bit "
"float RGB (HDR) and LMS, as well as a set of painterly colorspaces that "
"compute color mixing using the Kubelka-munk equations, which, in plain words "
"means that if you mix yellow and blue you get green, not purple."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: introduction.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "Image formats"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&krita; currently supports the following image formats, both for importing "
"and exporting, apart from its own: Raw, PNG, TIFF, JPEG, Dicom, XCF, PSD, "
"GIF, BMP, XPM, Targa, RGB, and OpenEXR. Additionally, &krita; can import ICO "
"files. PSD (the Photoshop file format) is only supported up to version 6, "
"from version 7 on, the Photoshop file format is closed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Embedded icc profiles and exif information are preserved on export to "
"supporting file formats. &krita;'s native file format stores icc and exif "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&krita; supports import and export of not just exif metadata, but also xmp."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: introduction.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "About this manual"
msgstr "អំពី​សៀវភៅ​ដៃ​នេះ"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We are assuming you have got a good working knowledge of &kde; and of your "
"operating system. The first chapter will give you a quick tour of &krita;'s "
"cool features; the other chapters will expand on that information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This manual is not complete. The invitation to join us and help out extends "
"to the manual, too!"
msgstr ""
"សៀវភៅ​ដៃ​នេះមិនទាន់​បញ្ចប់​នូវ​ឡើយ​ទេ ។ លិខិត​អញ្ជើញ​ចូលរួម​ជាមួយ​ពួក​យើង និង​ជួយ​ពង្រីក​សៀវភៅ​ដៃ ​ផង​ដែរ ។​"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:167
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Should you have any questions, comments or suggestions, please contact "
#| "the documentation maintainer at <email>sanderkoning@kde.nl</email>."
msgid ""
"Should you have any questions, comments or suggestions, please contact the "
"documentation maintainer at <email>boud@kde.org</email>."
msgstr ""
"បើ​មាន​សំណួរ សេចក្តី​អធិប្បាយ ឬ​ការ​ផ្តល់​មត្តិ​យោបលសូម​ទាក់ទង​ជាមួយ​អ្នកថែទាំតាម​អ៊ីមែល "
"<email>sanderkoning@kde.nl</email> ។"

#. Tag: title
#: introduction.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "About the application maintainer"
msgstr "អំពី​អ្នក​ថែទាំ​កម្មវិធី"

#. Tag: para
#: introduction.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Hi! I'm Boudewijn Rempt &mdash; the current maintainer of &krita;. I was "
"educated as a linguist, retrained as a database developer, work as a C++ "
"hacker, and I have always liked to paint and sketch a little. Conspicuously "
"absent in my life have been two important things for a developer of an image "
"app: mathematics and experience with graphic design. That means that I am "
"probably not the best person to explain the niceties of using an image "
"editor or a paint application to you. If you catch me in an error, please "
"don't hesitate to mail me: <email>boud@valdyas.org</email>."
msgstr ""

